# Publishing a report

This site is static. GitHub Pages serves the `main` branch root at https://cybercyberlabs.com/. Pages does not build the feed, so the generated files have to be committed.

When adding a report:

1. Add `reports/<slug>.html` in the existing Vim reader layout. Link `../report.css`, `../report.js`, and `<link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="CyberCyber Labs" href="../feed.xml">`.
2. Add the PDF under `reports/`.
3. Add an entry at the top of `publications.json` with `label`, `title`, `summary`, `published` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `html`, and `pdf`.
4. Rebuild the feed and the homepage list before committing:

```bash
python3 scripts/build_feed.py
```

5. Commit `publications.json`, `feed.xml`, and `publications.js` with the report. Do not edit `feed.xml` or `publications.js` by hand, and do not add the report only in `index.html`.
6. Push to `main` to deploy.

`publications.js` is what the homepage and the `work` command render. `feed.xml` is https://cybercyberlabs.com/feed.xml.
